  </ul>

  <h2>3. No Claims of Cure or Treatment</h2>
  <p>The Course does not claim to diagnose, treat, cure, mitigate, or prevent any disease or medical condition. The information provided is designed to support general wellness habits and behavioral adjustments that may improve sleep quality for individuals who do not have underlying clinical sleep disorders.</p>
  <p>We make no guarantees, representations, or warranties that the Course will produce any specific results. Individual experiences and outcomes vary significantly depending on personal circumstances, health conditions, lifestyle factors, and the degree of implementation.</p>

  <h2>4. Consult Your Healthcare Provider</h2>
  <p><strong>You should always consult with a qualified healthcare professional before:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Starting any new wellness, lifestyle, or behavioral change program</li>
    <li>Making changes to your sleep schedule, particularly if you operate heavy machinery, drive, or perform safety-sensitive work</li>
    <li>Reducing, changing, or discontinuing any medication, including sleep aids, supplements, or other prescriptions</li>
    <li>Implementing any dietary changes suggested in the Course (such as caffeine reduction protocols)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Who Should NOT Rely on This Course</h2>
  <p>This Course is designed for generally healthy adults experiencing lifestyle-related sleep difficulties. <strong>The Course is NOT appropriate as a primary intervention for individuals who:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Have been diagnosed with or suspect they have a clinical sleep disorder (insomnia disorder, sleep apnea, narcolepsy, parasomnias, etc.)</li>
    <li>Are currently undergoing treatment for a sleep disorder or mental health condition that significantly affects sleep</li>
    <li>Experience severe, chronic insomnia that has persisted for more than 3 months and significantly impairs daily functioning</li>
    <li>Are taking prescription sleep medications and considering changing their medication regimen</li>
    <li>Are pregnant, nursing, or have significant medical conditions that affect sleep</li>
    <li>Have been advised by a healthcare professional to follow a specific medical sleep protocol</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If any of the above applies to you, we strongly recommend that you consult a licensed healthcare provider or sleep specialist before using this Course.</p>

